WEBVTT


00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.000
Downloaded @ subs4free.club


00:00:28.868 --> 00:00:31.203
<i>There are legends
of people...</i>


00:00:31.236 --> 00:00:35.440
<i>born with the gift
of making music so true...</i>


00:00:35.474 --> 00:00:41.113
<i>it can pierce the veil
between life and death.</i>


00:00:41.146 --> 00:00:46.619
<i>Conjuring spirits
from the past and the future.</i>


00:00:46.653 --> 00:00:49.388
<i>In ancient Ireland,
they were called Filí.</i>


00:00:49.421 --> 00:00:51.758
<i>♪ The Lord above ♪</i>


00:00:51.791 --> 00:00:54.794
<i>In Choctaw land,
they call them firekeepers.</i>


00:00:56.361 --> 00:00:58.698
<i>And in West Africa...</i>


00:00:58.731 --> 00:01:02.134
<i>they're called griots.</i>


00:01:02.167 --> 00:01:07.205
<i>This gift can bring healing
to their communities...</i>


00:01:07.239 --> 00:01:11.209
<i>but it also attracts evil.</i>


00:01:56.723 --> 00:02:00.560
<i>♪ This little light of mine ♪</i>


00:02:00.593 --> 00:02:04.731
<i>♪ I'm gonna let it shine ♪</i>


00:02:04.764 --> 00:02:08.367
<i>♪ This little light of mine ♪</i>


00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:11.838
<i>♪ I'm gonna let it shine ♪</i>


00:02:11.871 --> 00:02:15.608
<i>♪ This little light of mine ♪</i>


00:02:15.642 --> 00:02:19.444
<i>♪ I'm gonna let it shine
Let it shine ♪</i>


00:02:19.478 --> 00:02:21.714
- Sammie!
- Ruthie.


00:02:21.748 --> 00:02:22.815
No, no.


00:02:26.284 --> 00:02:27.252
Come on, son.


00:02:30.255 --> 00:02:31.256
It's okay.


00:02:34.326 --> 00:02:35.528
-Sammie!
-My son has felt


00:02:35.561 --> 00:02:36.596
the call of sin.


00:02:39.832 --> 00:02:42.367
But the good Lord calls upon us


00:02:42.401 --> 00:02:45.237
to be fishers of men who sin...


00:02:46.839 --> 00:02:48.340
and show them the way.


00:02:56.816 --> 00:02:58.651
I want you to swear to me,


00:02:58.685 --> 00:03:00.753
and before this congregation...


00:03:00.787 --> 00:03:04.423
to leave those sinnin' ways
where they lie.


00:03:05.825 --> 00:03:07.927
I want you
to promise, right now.


00:03:11.030 --> 00:03:13.599
Drop the guitar, Samuel.


00:03:17.770 --> 00:03:18.738
In the name of God.


00:03:24.510 --> 00:03:25.645
Let it go, Samuel.


00:03:28.548 --> 00:03:29.682
Put it down.


00:03:51.904 --> 00:03:53.405
<i>♪ Somebody ♪</i>


00:03:56.843 --> 00:03:59.612
<i>♪ In your arms tonight ♪</i>


00:04:00.880 --> 00:04:02.648
<i>♪ Somebody take me ♪</i>


00:04:02.682 --> 00:04:05.651
You strummin'
that guitar tonight?


00:04:05.685 --> 00:04:07.053
Good mornin',
Miss Beatrice.


00:04:07.086 --> 00:04:08.821
You gonna tell me
where you playin'


00:04:08.855 --> 00:04:11.023
or am I gonna have to hear it
through the grapevine?


00:04:11.057 --> 00:04:12.692
You have
a good one, Beatrice.


00:04:12.725 --> 00:04:15.061
I'll see you at service
tomorrow morning.


00:04:15.094 --> 00:04:16.863
I guess
the grapevine it is.


00:04:29.008 --> 00:04:30.576
Mornin', Ma.


00:04:30.610 --> 00:04:31.611
Mornin', baby.


00:04:35.648 --> 00:04:37.049
Don't put that
on your body, Samuel.


00:04:37.083 --> 00:04:38.350
Come on, Ma. Soap is soap.


00:04:38.383 --> 00:04:39.619
It'll dry ya out.


00:04:39.652 --> 00:04:41.988
I'll put this on
while it's still wet.


00:04:42.021 --> 00:04:43.488
Boy, you ain't got the sense


00:04:43.523 --> 00:04:44.757
God gave a goose.


00:04:44.791 --> 00:04:46.592
<i>Go on. Get.</i>


00:04:46.626 --> 00:04:47.827
- Hey,
Mama said get up.


00:04:49.562 --> 00:04:50.897
Morning, Sammie.


00:04:52.799 --> 00:04:54.000
Don't wanna wake.


00:06:12.044 --> 00:06:13.112
You Hogwood?


00:06:17.917 --> 00:06:18.918
You boys twins?


00:06:20.219 --> 00:06:21.621
Nah,
we cousins.


00:06:22.822 --> 00:06:24.023
Well.


00:06:24.056 --> 00:06:26.158
Here she is.


00:06:26.192 --> 00:06:28.961
He moved a ton of timber
a month back in his heyday.


00:06:28.995 --> 00:06:30.696
Workers lived upstairs.


00:06:30.730 --> 00:06:32.598
Say,


00:06:32.632 --> 00:06:34.466
what are you fellas planning
on doing with the place?


00:06:40.172 --> 00:06:41.707
Y'all washed these floors?


00:06:42.742 --> 00:06:43.776
Yeah.


00:06:43.809 --> 00:06:44.777
What was on 'em?


00:06:48.014 --> 00:06:50.149
I thought y'all was
dead set on buying the place.


00:06:51.517 --> 00:06:52.985
More time I spend with y'all,


00:06:53.019 --> 00:06:54.720
the less sure I am
you boys are serious about it.


00:06:56.255 --> 00:06:58.024
Ain't no "boys" here.


00:06:58.057 --> 00:06:59.659
Just grown men.


00:06:59.692 --> 00:07:01.027
With grown-men money.


00:07:01.060 --> 00:07:02.494
And grown-men bullets.


00:07:17.143 --> 00:07:18.644
I didn't mean nothin' by it.


00:07:19.979 --> 00:07:21.647
Just the way we talk down here.


00:07:22.248 --> 00:07:23.448
We'll take it.


00:07:25.818 --> 00:07:27.053
The mill, the equipment,


00:07:27.086 --> 00:07:28.854
and the land
that it's standing on.


00:07:30.723 --> 00:07:31.891
Well, damn.


00:07:31.924 --> 00:07:33.626
Now, understand,
it's the last dime


00:07:33.659 --> 00:07:35.061
you ever gonna see from us.


00:07:35.094 --> 00:07:36.228
And if we see you,


00:07:36.262 --> 00:07:38.064
or any one of your Klan buddies


00:07:38.097 --> 00:07:39.932
cross our property line,


00:07:39.966 --> 00:07:41.600
we gonna kill 'em
right where they stand.


00:07:42.868 --> 00:07:44.603
Shit.


00:07:44.637 --> 00:07:46.238
Klan don't exist no more.


00:08:04.657 --> 00:08:05.658
Mornin', Pop.


00:08:07.326 --> 00:08:08.794
You're up awful early, son.


00:08:08.828 --> 00:08:10.096
Like you say...


00:08:10.129 --> 00:08:11.530
"Jump on the work,


00:08:11.564 --> 00:08:12.531
don't let the work
jump on you."


00:08:12.565 --> 00:08:13.599
That's right.


00:08:13.632 --> 00:08:15.101
Finished my quota for the day.


00:08:20.106 --> 00:08:23.109
Yeah. I brought it in here.


00:08:23.142 --> 00:08:25.678
I want you to help me
give my sermon tomorrow.


00:08:30.049 --> 00:08:32.785
First Corinthians, 10:13.


00:08:35.921 --> 00:08:36.922
Read.


00:08:38.190 --> 00:08:40.126
"No temptation...


00:08:40.159 --> 00:08:41.894
has overtaken you,


00:08:41.927 --> 00:08:44.030
except what is common
to mankind.


00:08:44.063 --> 00:08:45.297
God is faithful.


00:08:46.966 --> 00:08:48.167
He will not let you be tempted


00:08:48.200 --> 00:08:49.535
beyond what you can bear.


00:08:50.803 --> 00:08:51.937
But when you're tempted...


00:08:51.971 --> 00:08:53.005
he will also provide a way out


00:08:53.039 --> 00:08:55.341
so that you can endure it."


00:08:55.374 --> 00:08:57.877
Now, Pop, if you don't mind,
I'm gon' be late.


00:08:57.910 --> 00:08:58.778
Late for what, boy?


00:09:00.679 --> 00:09:01.947
Where you gotta be
that's more important


00:09:01.981 --> 00:09:03.215
than being in the House of God?


00:09:05.651 --> 00:09:07.319
I been workin' all week, Pop.


00:09:10.022 --> 00:09:12.124
Wanna be free
of all this for a day.


00:09:12.158 --> 00:09:13.192
To play music?


00:09:14.627 --> 00:09:16.162
For drunkards?


00:09:16.195 --> 00:09:17.997
Philanderers, who shirk
their responsibilities


00:09:18.030 --> 00:09:19.265
to their families


00:09:19.298 --> 00:09:20.966
so they can sweat
all over each other?


00:09:22.768 --> 00:09:24.770
I'll be back in time
for service in the morning.


00:09:27.173 --> 00:09:28.207
Son?


00:09:33.379 --> 00:09:35.314
You keep dancing
with the devil...


00:09:37.316 --> 00:09:39.218
one day,
he's gonna follow you home.


00:09:43.222 --> 00:09:44.723
Hey, lil' cousin,
come on out.


00:09:46.225 --> 00:09:48.160
Got two dollars out here
waitin' on a dime.


00:09:49.295 --> 00:09:50.296
Samuel!


00:09:54.100 --> 00:09:57.169
Aw, don't you worry now,
Uncle Jed.


00:09:57.203 --> 00:09:59.038
We gon' get him back to you
in one piece.


00:10:07.179 --> 00:10:08.747
Well, how you be?


00:10:08.781 --> 00:10:11.684
Your daddy doin' right by you?


00:10:11.717 --> 00:10:13.052
Say, he not putting his hands
on you, is he?


00:10:13.085 --> 00:10:14.920
Nah, man. Nothin' too much.


00:10:16.188 --> 00:10:17.423
What about the little ones?


00:10:17.456 --> 00:10:19.291
Only when they deserve it.


00:10:19.325 --> 00:10:21.861
Well, Ma usually
hands out the whoopin's.


00:10:21.894 --> 00:10:24.930
Good. Well, Uncle Jed
always been good.


00:10:24.964 --> 00:10:25.965
Yeah.


00:10:27.299 --> 00:10:29.235
So, tell me about Chicago.


00:10:29.268 --> 00:10:31.203
I heard they ain't got
Jim Crow up there.


00:10:32.438 --> 00:10:35.841
Black man can go
where he wants.


00:10:35.875 --> 00:10:37.243
Listen, boy, you can't
be believin' everything


00:10:37.276 --> 00:10:39.211
that you hear.


00:10:39.245 --> 00:10:41.213
Town'll fill your head up
with this make-believe,


00:10:41.247 --> 00:10:42.748
but me and your cousin,


00:10:42.781 --> 00:10:44.150
we gon' give it
to you straight.


00:10:45.151 --> 00:10:46.418
Chicago ain't shit


00:10:46.452 --> 00:10:47.820
but Mississippi
with tall buildings


00:10:47.853 --> 00:10:49.021
instead of plantations.


00:10:51.957 --> 00:10:54.093
And that's why
we came back home.


00:10:54.126 --> 00:10:56.362
Figured we might as well
deal with the devil we know.


00:11:33.165 --> 00:11:34.800
Don't move.


00:11:47.880 --> 00:11:49.381
How 'bout you leave
that truck to us?


00:11:58.824 --> 00:12:00.326
Shit. Cracker showin' up late


00:12:00.359 --> 00:12:02.928
already got us behind schedule.


00:12:02.962 --> 00:12:04.463
I'm thinkin'
we just set up tonight.


00:12:04.496 --> 00:12:05.998
Open up next weekend.


00:12:06.031 --> 00:12:07.967
Nah, fuck that.
It's gotta be tonight.


00:12:08.000 --> 00:12:10.102
Grand opening,
start this shit with a bang.


00:12:10.135 --> 00:12:11.337
Or we start with a misfire.


00:12:12.304 --> 00:12:13.239
Look at that sky.


00:12:15.107 --> 00:12:17.142
That's a mighty fine day
to be free, ain't it?


00:12:18.143 --> 00:12:20.246
Our own juke joint.


00:12:20.279 --> 00:12:22.248
For us, and by us.


00:12:22.281 --> 00:12:24.049
Just like we always wanted.


00:12:27.953 --> 00:12:30.289
Only chance we got
if we split up.


00:12:30.322 --> 00:12:31.857
Well, who gon' watch the truck


00:12:31.890 --> 00:12:33.125
while I'm in there
talking to the Chows?


00:12:33.158 --> 00:12:34.426
Nigga, just let 'em
see it's you.


00:12:34.460 --> 00:12:36.161
We've been gone
a long time, Stack.


00:12:36.195 --> 00:12:37.763
Seven years ain't long enough
to forget about us.


00:12:38.864 --> 00:12:41.000
All right.


00:12:41.033 --> 00:12:43.302
Watch this fool. Make sure
he don't get in no trouble.


00:12:43.335 --> 00:12:45.204
You big enough
to take me now, huh?


00:12:45.237 --> 00:12:46.372
I'll do what I can.


00:12:46.405 --> 00:12:48.841
Nah, you'll do what you told.


00:12:48.874 --> 00:12:50.976
You keep your eyes open
for anybody staring too long.


00:12:51.010 --> 00:12:52.978
This nigga don't know
how to watch his own back.


00:12:55.080 --> 00:12:56.115
-I love you.
-I love you, too.


00:12:56.148 --> 00:12:57.550
-Be careful.
-I will.


00:13:01.453 --> 00:13:02.522
You with me.


00:14:07.554 --> 00:14:08.555
Hey, little girl.


00:14:10.389 --> 00:14:11.423
Come here.


00:14:14.293 --> 00:14:15.427
Where you from?


00:14:15.461 --> 00:14:16.895
Shelby.


00:14:16.929 --> 00:14:18.163
You heard of
the Smokestack Twins?


00:14:18.197 --> 00:14:19.365
Of course.


00:14:19.398 --> 00:14:21.300
Good. I'm Smoke.


00:14:23.001 --> 00:14:25.304
No, no, no, now.
You're not in no trouble.


00:14:25.337 --> 00:14:28.575
See, I'm trying to put
some money in your pocket.


00:14:28.608 --> 00:14:32.111
See, I'mma need you to come
sit in this truck right here.


00:14:32.144 --> 00:14:34.514
And if somebody come
and look a little too long...


00:14:34.547 --> 00:14:36.315
I want you to lean
on this horn, all right?


00:14:36.348 --> 00:14:37.416
Can you do that for me?


00:14:39.084 --> 00:14:40.953
Can you tell time?


00:14:40.986 --> 00:14:42.454
I'mma pay you ten cents


00:14:42.488 --> 00:14:44.390
for every minute that I'm gone.


00:14:44.423 --> 00:14:46.358
-Will that work for you?
-Yes, sir.


00:14:46.392 --> 00:14:47.993
No, ma'am.


00:14:48.026 --> 00:14:49.696
See, we talkin' numbers now.


00:14:49.729 --> 00:14:52.665
And numbers always gotta be in
conversation with each other.


00:14:52.699 --> 00:14:54.032
You understand?


00:14:54.066 --> 00:14:55.668
You gotta negotiate.


00:14:55.702 --> 00:14:59.304
Now, ten cents
just won't work for you.


00:14:59.338 --> 00:15:01.440
Talk another number back to me.


00:15:01.473 --> 00:15:02.509
Fitty cent.


00:15:02.542 --> 00:15:05.110
Twenty cents. Best I can do.


00:15:05.144 --> 00:15:06.945
We got a deal?


00:15:06.979 --> 00:15:08.280
Good. Jump in.


00:15:13.085 --> 00:15:14.554
Remember, lean on that horn.


00:15:36.576 --> 00:15:38.410
You not little Lisa, is you?


00:15:38.444 --> 00:15:40.012
Guilty as charged.


00:15:40.045 --> 00:15:41.280
- Mornin', Sarah.
- Mornin'!


00:15:41.313 --> 00:15:43.315
-Your daddy here?
-Daddy!


00:15:44.383 --> 00:15:45.317
What?


00:15:47.052 --> 00:15:48.287
Bo Chow.


00:15:48.320 --> 00:15:50.122
Look what the damn cat
dragged in.


00:15:54.259 --> 00:15:55.494
What can I do for you?


00:15:55.528 --> 00:15:57.196
We throwin'
a big event tonight.


00:15:57.229 --> 00:15:58.363
- What do you need?
- I need catfish


00:15:58.397 --> 00:15:59.599
for a hundred people.


00:15:59.632 --> 00:16:00.600
Y'all do good
up in Chicago?


00:16:00.633 --> 00:16:01.768
I heard about some of them


00:16:01.801 --> 00:16:03.035
casinos up there.
Y'all hit it big?


00:16:06.371 --> 00:16:07.406
We hit.


00:16:07.439 --> 00:16:08.641
Just not the way you thinking.


00:16:09.408 --> 00:16:10.543
What kind of way?


00:16:12.344 --> 00:16:13.613
Shit.


00:16:19.552 --> 00:16:21.554
- They stealin'!
- Mm-hm.


00:16:21.588 --> 00:16:23.489
Watch my fingers, fool.


00:16:23.523 --> 00:16:25.123
I'm trying to make sure
they ain't watchin' that shit.


00:16:25.157 --> 00:16:27.092
Man, just get
your own damn thing, bro.


00:16:27.125 --> 00:16:27.760
- I'm trying to help you.
-  -Watch it, man.


00:16:29.061 --> 00:16:30.295
Fuck you going, nigga?


00:16:30.329 --> 00:16:31.363
Bet this bullet'll
beat you there.


00:16:32.565 --> 00:16:35.334
You shot me. Mother...


00:16:37.737 --> 00:16:39.338
Smoke.


00:16:39.371 --> 00:16:41.574
Terry? Boy, how you been?


00:16:41.608 --> 00:16:44.176
I was doin' better
'fore you shot me in the ass.


00:16:44.209 --> 00:16:45.545
Why in the hell you trying
to boost from my truck?


00:16:45.578 --> 00:16:47.547
This your truck?


00:16:47.580 --> 00:16:48.648
I didn't know
it was your truck.


00:16:48.681 --> 00:16:49.782
-I swear, Smoke.
-Bullshit.


00:16:49.816 --> 00:16:51.518
I told you it was his.


00:16:51.551 --> 00:16:53.252
Wait, wait, Smoke. I thought,
I thought she was lyin'.


00:16:53.285 --> 00:16:55.153
Y'all was supposed to be
in Chicago workin' for Capone.


00:16:57.189 --> 00:16:58.223
Yeah, we back now.


00:17:05.765 --> 00:17:08.701
Goddamn! What you do that for?


00:17:08.735 --> 00:17:10.235
Can't have
some nigga talkin' about


00:17:10.269 --> 00:17:12.170
how he almost robbed the Twins.


00:17:12.204 --> 00:17:13.573
Not without a limp
to show for it.


00:17:13.606 --> 00:17:15.173
- Well, who gon' patch me up?
- Shit!


00:17:15.207 --> 00:17:16.543
I ain't got no money.


00:17:16.576 --> 00:17:18.277
What if I get sepsis
or some shit in the ass?


00:17:18.310 --> 00:17:20.345
Y'all scoot on out the street.
Put some pressure on it.


00:17:22.515 --> 00:17:24.584
- Get up, boy.
- Nigga, I need help!


00:17:24.617 --> 00:17:26.519
Get up, fool.
Get out the street.


00:17:28.821 --> 00:17:30.188
Doc Teddy
still live 'round here?


00:17:30.222 --> 00:17:31.423
Yeah.


00:17:31.456 --> 00:17:33.158
I just shot
a couple niggas outside.


00:17:33.191 --> 00:17:36.395
If they gon' live, they gon'
need some patching up.


00:17:36.428 --> 00:17:37.764
Yeah,
we can take care of that.


00:17:37.797 --> 00:17:38.798
Anything else?


00:17:40.232 --> 00:17:42.535
Yeah, we gon' need a sign too.


00:17:42.569 --> 00:17:44.504
You think Grace'd be
up to making us one?


00:17:44.537 --> 00:17:45.838
When would you need it done?


00:17:45.872 --> 00:17:47.574
Tonight.


00:17:47.607 --> 00:17:49.374
Lisa. Go get your mama.


00:17:52.277 --> 00:17:55.247
<i>Y'all gon' have food,
drink, music.</i>


00:17:55.280 --> 00:17:57.115
<i>Is y'all gon' be playing?</i>


00:17:57.149 --> 00:17:59.852
<i>You say. Cards, dice,
even got a roulette.</i>


00:18:07.694 --> 00:18:09.596
Do nothing
but shoot each other up.


00:18:09.629 --> 00:18:11.430
Glory be,


00:18:11.463 --> 00:18:13.800
I have no animosity towards
colored folk, but if they...


00:18:13.833 --> 00:18:16.368
Mama, Daddy wants you.


00:18:16.401 --> 00:18:17.469
- Thank you.
- Thank you.


00:18:20.472 --> 00:18:22.742
Used to be that
they had their side of town


00:18:22.775 --> 00:18:23.843
and we had ours.


00:18:38.591 --> 00:18:39.826
I can't feel my leg,


00:18:39.859 --> 00:18:42.361
I'm gonna have to hop
all around town!


00:18:42.394 --> 00:18:43.663
Oh, yeah.


00:18:43.696 --> 00:18:45.732
We definitely
oughta try bring him.


00:18:45.765 --> 00:18:48.835
You know,
there's two men out there,


00:18:48.868 --> 00:18:50.235
look like they been shot.


00:18:50.268 --> 00:18:51.470
That'll be my doin'.


00:18:51.504 --> 00:18:52.605
I done already gave Bo
the money


00:18:52.639 --> 00:18:53.940
to get 'em patched up.


00:18:53.973 --> 00:18:55.775
Why you gotta come here
bringin' trouble?


00:18:55.808 --> 00:18:57.409
Trouble ain't
all he bringing.


00:18:58.377 --> 00:18:59.612
Jesus.


00:18:59.646 --> 00:19:00.947
How you payin' for this?


00:19:00.980 --> 00:19:03.583
And he wants you
to make a sign for him.


00:19:03.616 --> 00:19:05.484
Rush job. Gon' cost ya.


00:19:05.518 --> 00:19:06.819
I'm listenin'.


00:19:06.853 --> 00:19:08.621
Twenty.


00:19:08.655 --> 00:19:09.956
Fifteen for the front door
sign and five for the menu.


00:19:09.989 --> 00:19:11.289
Ten. Seven for
the front door sign,


00:19:11.323 --> 00:19:12.424
three for the menu.


00:19:12.457 --> 00:19:13.559
-Sixteen.
-Fifteen.


00:19:13.593 --> 00:19:14.894
Done.


00:19:14.927 --> 00:19:17.329
Oh. We only got
one color, by the way.


00:19:18.931 --> 00:19:20.432
What color you got?


00:19:20.465 --> 00:19:22.267
Red.


00:19:22.300 --> 00:19:24.169
-Thirteen.
-$14.50.


00:19:27.305 --> 00:19:30.442
Fourteen. Throw in these
flowers right here...


00:19:30.475 --> 00:19:31.443
and we got a deal.


00:19:32.444 --> 00:19:33.378
Done.


00:19:35.648 --> 00:19:36.649
Where's Stack?


00:19:36.683 --> 00:19:37.784
All right, listen.


00:19:37.817 --> 00:19:39.619
Every cooze got a button on it,


00:19:39.652 --> 00:19:40.987
towards the top.


00:19:41.020 --> 00:19:43.388
If you wanna keep a woman,
you find it...


00:19:44.289 --> 00:19:45.558
lick that.


00:19:45.591 --> 00:19:48.528
Not too hard.
Not too soft, either.


00:19:48.561 --> 00:19:50.495
You ever had a scoop of
that ice cream from downtown?


00:19:50.530 --> 00:19:51.798
Uh-huh.


00:19:51.831 --> 00:19:53.566
'Bout the same pressure
you put on that.


00:19:53.599 --> 00:19:55.367
Like it taste good,


00:19:55.400 --> 00:19:56.869
but you don't want it gone
too quickly, you understand?


00:19:58.370 --> 00:19:59.906
Hey, how fast this thing drive?


00:19:59.939 --> 00:20:01.206
Too damn fast.


00:20:01.974 --> 00:20:03.308
Why? You wanna drive?


00:20:03.341 --> 00:20:04.309
Come on, you know
I wanna drive.


00:20:04.342 --> 00:20:06.445
Later. On the way back.


00:20:06.478 --> 00:20:07.880
- On the way back.
- All right, all right.


00:20:10.282 --> 00:20:11.651
You always said
you would tell me


00:20:11.684 --> 00:20:13.485
what happened to your daddy
when I got older.


00:20:15.021 --> 00:20:16.221
Well, I guess I'm older.


00:20:19.592 --> 00:20:20.660
Y'all really kill him?


00:20:26.465 --> 00:20:27.734
Nah, we ain't kill him.


00:20:29.502 --> 00:20:30.402
Smoke did.


00:20:31.771 --> 00:20:33.973
Our daddy
knocked me unconscious.


00:20:34.006 --> 00:20:35.608
By the time I came to,


00:20:35.641 --> 00:20:37.009
Smoke was halfway done
buryin' him.


00:20:38.310 --> 00:20:39.377
He used to beat y'all?


00:20:39.411 --> 00:20:41.047
Me, mostly.


00:20:41.080 --> 00:20:42.347
But he ain't mean it.


00:20:45.051 --> 00:20:47.319
See you been takin'
good care of that thing.


00:20:49.088 --> 00:20:51.023
Hey, I can't thank y'all
enough for this.


00:20:51.858 --> 00:20:53.726
Plays so right.


00:20:53.760 --> 00:20:55.995
Where'd I get this from anyway?


00:20:56.028 --> 00:20:59.431
Yeah, that's, uh,
Charley Patton's guitar.


00:20:59.464 --> 00:21:01.000
Me and my brother
won it off him in a card game.


00:21:01.033 --> 00:21:02.400
Hold on, Stack.


00:21:03.770 --> 00:21:05.337
You mean to tell me


00:21:05.370 --> 00:21:06.304
I had Charley Patton's guitar
this whole time?


00:21:06.338 --> 00:21:07.372
Swear 'fore God,


00:21:07.405 --> 00:21:08.674
-in your hands.
-Nah.


00:21:08.708 --> 00:21:10.009
Now let's see
if you can play like him.


00:21:10.042 --> 00:21:11.309
-Right here?
-Yeah, right now. Come on.


00:21:11.343 --> 00:21:13.445
All right. Come on. Watch this.


00:21:29.662 --> 00:21:31.898
<i>♪ Traveling ♪</i>


00:21:31.931 --> 00:21:34.432
<i>♪ I don't know
Where in the world I'm goin' ♪</i>


00:21:38.436 --> 00:21:40.573
<i>♪ Traveling ♪</i>


00:21:40.606 --> 00:21:43.441
<i>♪ I don't know
Where in the world I'm goin' ♪</i>


00:21:43.475 --> 00:21:46.612
Hoo hoo, boy!


00:21:46.646 --> 00:21:48.815
<i>♪ 'Cause the woman
That I'm lovin' ♪</i>


00:21:48.848 --> 00:21:51.449
<i>♪ She sure
Don't feel like that ♪</i>


00:21:51.483 --> 00:21:54.887
We gon' make some money.
We gon' make some money.


00:22:15.608 --> 00:22:16.676
Let's go. Take hold.


00:22:19.879 --> 00:22:21.781
-Thanks, Twin.
-Yep.


00:22:23.149 --> 00:22:25.350
Oh. Is that Delta Slim?


00:22:34.894 --> 00:22:35.828
Delta Slim.


00:22:39.899 --> 00:22:42.034
Yeah, I thank you
for your generosity.


00:22:48.074 --> 00:22:50.576
I guess that Chicago wind


00:22:50.610 --> 00:22:52.912
blew your Black asses
back down here, huh?


00:22:54.847 --> 00:22:56.414
Who the boy?


00:22:56.448 --> 00:22:58.751
This my little cousin.
Preacherboy Sammie.


00:22:58.784 --> 00:23:03.155
Happens to be the finest
blues player in all the Delta.


00:23:03.189 --> 00:23:05.858
I got socks
older than this here boy.


00:23:07.159 --> 00:23:09.095
What the hell he know
about the blues?


00:23:14.133 --> 00:23:15.801
I can show you
better than I can tell you.


00:23:15.835 --> 00:23:17.937
Hold up, now.
Put that motherfucker...


00:23:17.970 --> 00:23:19.071
Put that away.


00:23:19.105 --> 00:23:20.573
Get, get.


00:23:20.606 --> 00:23:22.041
Now, this here my patch
right here.


00:23:22.074 --> 00:23:24.510
Now, you wasn't his cousin
and a young pup to boot,


00:23:24.543 --> 00:23:26.646
I'd cut your ass
too thin to fry.


00:23:26.679 --> 00:23:28.114
And you threaten him again...


00:23:28.147 --> 00:23:29.682
I'mma make your drunk ass
swallow that harmonica.


00:23:32.752 --> 00:23:34.754
You still nice with them keys?


00:23:34.787 --> 00:23:37.523
Depend on who you ask.


00:23:37.556 --> 00:23:41.160
I'll give you $20 to come play
at our juke tonight.


00:23:42.228 --> 00:23:44.130
Yeah, I wish I could.


00:23:44.163 --> 00:23:45.765
I'mma be
at Messenger's tonight,


00:23:45.798 --> 00:23:47.900
same as I am
every Saturday night.


00:23:47.934 --> 00:23:50.036
What they pay you?


00:23:50.069 --> 00:23:51.469
For a gangster,


00:23:51.504 --> 00:23:52.905
you sure ask
a lot of questions.


00:23:52.939 --> 00:23:54.874
They ain't paying you
$20 a night, I know that.


00:23:54.907 --> 00:23:56.642
You ain't paying
no $20 a night.


00:23:57.877 --> 00:24:00.478
You payin' $20, maybe, tonight.


00:24:02.515 --> 00:24:04.684
I ain't never heard
of your juke.


00:24:04.717 --> 00:24:07.853
Maybe it's here tonight,
is it here tomorrow night?


00:24:07.887 --> 00:24:10.523
The week after that? Nah.


00:24:10.556 --> 00:24:12.024
I been at Messenger's
every Saturday night


00:24:12.058 --> 00:24:13.726
for the last ten years.


00:24:13.759 --> 00:24:15.027
Messenger's gon' be there


00:24:15.061 --> 00:24:16.796
another ten years
after that, at least.


00:24:18.297 --> 00:24:19.765
Shit.


00:24:19.799 --> 00:24:22.201
That's probably
more time than I got


00:24:22.234 --> 00:24:23.936
left on this earth, Stack.


00:24:23.970 --> 00:24:27.540
I play, and I get as much
corn liquor as I can drink.


00:24:29.775 --> 00:24:30.843
A sinner like me,


00:24:30.876 --> 00:24:31.911
I can't ask for more than that.


00:24:34.547 --> 00:24:35.982
Know what, Slim?
I'll drink to that.


00:24:46.125 --> 00:24:47.126
Ooh.


00:24:48.794 --> 00:24:49.795
What you got there, boy?


00:24:49.829 --> 00:24:50.896
Oh, this?


00:24:51.764 --> 00:24:53.099
It's a Irish beer.


00:24:53.132 --> 00:24:55.701
Straight from the north side
of Chicago.


00:24:58.571 --> 00:24:59.972
You sayin' that's beer?


00:25:00.006 --> 00:25:01.974
Wind didn't bring us
down here empty-handed.


00:25:04.610 --> 00:25:05.878
Give me that.


00:25:15.755 --> 00:25:17.556
My goodness.


00:25:17.590 --> 00:25:20.159
I got 500 more bottles
just like that.


00:25:20.192 --> 00:25:21.293
Ice cold.


00:25:22.661 --> 00:25:24.030
Say we pay you $40 a night,


00:25:24.063 --> 00:25:25.831
and all the beer
that you can drink.


00:25:25.865 --> 00:25:27.633
After that, no strings.


00:25:27.666 --> 00:25:29.035
You act now,


00:25:29.068 --> 00:25:30.703
I'll even let you finish
that bottle in your hand.


00:25:33.039 --> 00:25:34.707
Ha!


00:25:41.947 --> 00:25:43.315
Ha!


00:25:43.349 --> 00:25:46.218
These two gon' be playin'
down at the old sawmill.


00:25:46.252 --> 00:25:48.587
It's the grand openin'
of our new joint.


00:25:48.621 --> 00:25:50.089
Club Juke.


00:25:50.122 --> 00:25:52.625
We gon' have us
a battle of the blues.


00:25:54.026 --> 00:25:56.028
It's gon' be
a real ring-a-ding-ding.


00:25:56.062 --> 00:25:57.229
Just for us.


00:26:14.013 --> 00:26:15.347
- Y'all ready to eat?
- Yeah!


00:26:15.381 --> 00:26:17.249
- Y'all ready to drank?
- Yeah!


00:26:17.283 --> 00:26:19.085
Y'all ready to sweat
till y'all stank?


00:26:19.118 --> 00:26:20.186
Yeah.


00:26:21.220 --> 00:26:22.922
All right.


00:26:22.955 --> 00:26:24.623
We gon' get funky like
a Mississippi donkey, y'all.


00:26:26.025 --> 00:26:28.294
Get a drink on the Twins
when you get there.


00:26:28.327 --> 00:26:30.162
I like it.
Where you get that one from?


00:26:30.196 --> 00:26:31.997
What I'm sayin', now.
Gotta do what you gotta do.


00:26:32.031 --> 00:26:33.032
You gotta.


00:26:34.166 --> 00:26:35.768
I've seen you somewhere before.


00:26:35.801 --> 00:26:37.303
Maybe.


00:26:38.170 --> 00:26:39.338
You sing, don't you?


00:26:40.840 --> 00:26:42.141
- Time to time.
- Mm-hm.


00:26:42.174 --> 00:26:43.642
I'm Preacherboy.


00:26:48.180 --> 00:26:49.215
Pearline.


00:26:50.216 --> 00:26:51.851
Pearline. Mm.


00:26:52.985 --> 00:26:54.120
I'm married, by the way.


00:26:54.753 --> 00:26:56.255
Happily?


00:26:56.288 --> 00:26:58.190
Careful, boy.


00:26:58.224 --> 00:27:00.292
You gon' bite off
more than you can chew.


00:27:03.195 --> 00:27:04.730
Maybe I'll
see you tonight.


00:27:12.004 --> 00:27:13.372
Then we'll take it
from there.


00:27:13.405 --> 00:27:15.007
I'mma hold you
to that, now.


00:27:15.040 --> 00:27:16.408
It's gonna be a night
you never forget.


00:27:16.442 --> 00:27:17.676
Hey, let me
go see about my money.


00:27:17.710 --> 00:27:19.378
Hey, go on and get your money.


00:27:19.411 --> 00:27:19.778
Hey, hey, hey.
There's a white woman
staring at you.


00:27:21.013 --> 00:27:22.348
Shit.


00:27:22.381 --> 00:27:24.150
Uh, you sure she white?


00:27:26.051 --> 00:27:27.453
She walkin' over here
right now.


00:27:27.486 --> 00:27:28.954
All right, now here's
what we're gonna do...


00:27:28.988 --> 00:27:30.756
Excuse me, boy.
Is this here Smoke?


00:27:31.857 --> 00:27:33.125
Or is this Stack?


00:27:33.159 --> 00:27:34.360
Don't... Don't look at her.


00:27:34.393 --> 00:27:36.695
Just go over there
and keep playing.


00:27:36.729 --> 00:27:37.930
Yeah, it's okay.


00:27:40.933 --> 00:27:42.935
-You know I waited for you.
-Yeah, well,


00:27:42.968 --> 00:27:44.203
I don't know why in the hell
you'd go and do that.


00:27:44.236 --> 00:27:46.071
Because you told me
you loved me.


00:27:46.105 --> 00:27:47.406
Yeah, well, I told you to stay
the fuck away from me, too,


00:27:47.439 --> 00:27:48.707
but I guess
you didn't hear that part.


00:27:48.741 --> 00:27:49.842
I heard you.


00:27:50.876 --> 00:27:52.244
I heard you loud and clear,


00:27:52.278 --> 00:27:53.345
but then you stuck your tongue
in my cooze


00:27:53.379 --> 00:27:54.947
and fucked me so hard,


00:27:54.980 --> 00:27:56.081
I figured
you changed your mind.


00:27:56.115 --> 00:27:57.917
Keep your voice down, now.


00:27:57.950 --> 00:27:59.885
It's not exactly how
I remember it.


00:27:59.919 --> 00:28:01.320
Oh, it ain't?
Remember falling asleep


00:28:01.353 --> 00:28:02.788
with your head on my chest?


00:28:02.821 --> 00:28:04.156
Leaving in the middle
of the night


00:28:04.190 --> 00:28:05.424
without a fucking word?


00:28:05.457 --> 00:28:07.026
The hell are you doing
back here, Mary?


00:28:08.961 --> 00:28:10.462
I buried my mama
yesterday, Stack.


00:28:12.532 --> 00:28:14.066
Figured I might see you
and Smoke there,


00:28:14.099 --> 00:28:15.768
as much as she looked
after you both.


00:28:15.801 --> 00:28:17.203
But I guess y'all love lasted


00:28:17.236 --> 00:28:18.037
as long as y'all could
get something out of her.


00:28:18.070 --> 00:28:19.405
You right.


00:28:19.438 --> 00:28:20.873
That's all she was.


00:28:20.906 --> 00:28:23.275
Food, a warm bed.


00:28:25.344 --> 00:28:27.146
Rot in hell, Stack.


00:28:27.179 --> 00:28:28.714
Shit, I will.


00:28:31.984 --> 00:28:34.253
You know, and save
your triflin' ass a room.


00:28:34.286 --> 00:28:37.289
Shit, right next to me. Shit.


00:28:37.323 --> 00:28:38.324
Hey, Stack.


00:28:39.358 --> 00:28:40.392
Hmm?


00:28:41.561 --> 00:28:42.728
Maybe she ain't white.


00:28:43.495 --> 00:28:44.830
Boy, let's get to gettin'.


00:28:44.863 --> 00:28:46.098
Come on, Slim.


00:28:46.131 --> 00:28:47.333
Still got
one more stop to make.


00:28:53.906 --> 00:28:56.442
<i>♪ Raise 'em up together ♪</i>


00:28:56.475 --> 00:28:57.876
<i>♪ Oh, my Lord ♪</i>


00:28:57.910 --> 00:28:59.512
Hold up.


00:28:59.546 --> 00:29:00.846
Slow down, Stack. Slow down.


00:29:00.879 --> 00:29:03.382
<i>♪ Rally can't hold me ♪</i>


00:29:04.850 --> 00:29:07.820
<i>♪ Rally can't hold me ♪</i>


00:29:07.853 --> 00:29:09.154
<i>♪ Rally can't hold me ♪</i>


00:29:09.188 --> 00:29:11.223
Y'all hold your heads now,
you hear me?


00:29:11.257 --> 00:29:13.092
<i>- Hold your heads!
- ♪ Oh, my Lord ♪</i>


00:29:13.125 --> 00:29:14.493
Slim!


00:29:19.131 --> 00:29:20.366
Hey, you knew some of them?


00:29:23.402 --> 00:29:24.403
All of 'em.


00:29:26.372 --> 00:29:27.273
What happened?


00:29:33.078 --> 00:29:34.480
Me and my buddy Rice...


00:29:36.315 --> 00:29:38.384
we was hustlin' back and forth
up the Delta.


00:29:38.417 --> 00:29:41.287
We get busted for vagrancy.


00:29:41.320 --> 00:29:43.889
Them white sheriffs
take us down to the jailhouse


00:29:43.922 --> 00:29:45.024
and it's empty.


00:29:46.626 --> 00:29:48.327
Thought for sure
they gon' kill us that night.


00:29:50.563 --> 00:29:51.930
They give us
our instruments back,


00:29:51.964 --> 00:29:53.165
they tell us to play.


00:29:53.198 --> 00:29:54.466
Stack, we played,


00:29:54.500 --> 00:29:57.002
Preacherboy, we played,
you hear me?


00:29:57.036 --> 00:29:59.038
Music was comin' out
the windows.


00:29:59.071 --> 00:30:01.473
Peoples on the street
were stoppin' to come on in.


00:30:03.375 --> 00:30:04.544
Next day, one of them sheriffs,


00:30:04.577 --> 00:30:06.011
they get the bright idea


00:30:06.045 --> 00:30:08.147
they gonna take us
on the road now.


00:30:08.180 --> 00:30:09.948
They cover us,
throw us in the paddy wagon.


00:30:11.417 --> 00:30:13.385
They took us to this big house.


00:30:13.419 --> 00:30:16.955
I mean,
it's full of white folks.


00:30:16.989 --> 00:30:19.024
Pass around their hat
and have us to play.


00:30:19.058 --> 00:30:21.493
See, these white folks
we were playing for,


00:30:21.528 --> 00:30:23.929
they had real money.


00:30:23.962 --> 00:30:25.565
Had y'all playing them
old ragtime songs?


00:30:25.598 --> 00:30:27.499
I sure was.


00:30:27.534 --> 00:30:30.135
We play
a fair amount of blues, too.


00:30:30.169 --> 00:30:32.204
See, white folks,
they like the blues just fine.


00:30:32.237 --> 00:30:34.106
They just don't like
the people who make it.


00:30:35.575 --> 00:30:37.443
Them peckerwoods
was noddin' their heads,


00:30:37.476 --> 00:30:39.178
stompin' their feet.


00:30:39.211 --> 00:30:41.548
Some of 'em was almost
on the rhythm, Stack.


00:30:43.349 --> 00:30:45.417
And then Rice and me,
we changed it up, confuse 'em.


00:30:48.120 --> 00:30:49.355
What did y'all do
with the money?


00:30:51.223 --> 00:30:52.224
I drank it.


00:30:53.992 --> 00:30:56.295
Rice said he was gonna
take that money...


00:30:56.328 --> 00:30:58.497
go on out to Little Rock,
start him a little church.


00:30:58.531 --> 00:30:59.532
Did he?


00:31:02.101 --> 00:31:04.470
The damn fool.


00:31:04.504 --> 00:31:06.539
He took out
all his money to pay


00:31:08.006 --> 00:31:09.475
for the $2 train ticket.


00:31:09.509 --> 00:31:11.176
Train conductor saw him...


00:31:11.210 --> 00:31:13.178
<i>That Black sumbitch
right there.</i>


00:31:13.212 --> 00:31:14.614
<i>- ...Klan got ahold to him.
- Pull him over here!</i>


00:31:14.647 --> 00:31:15.648
Searched his pockets,
found all that money.


00:31:15.682 --> 00:31:17.916
Made up a story about him...


00:31:17.950 --> 00:31:19.184
killin' some white man for it


00:31:19.218 --> 00:31:20.452
and rapin'
that white man's wife.


00:31:20.486 --> 00:31:22.020
<i>That boy's a murderer.</i>


00:31:22.054 --> 00:31:23.255
And they lynched him


00:31:23.288 --> 00:31:24.923
right there
in the railroad station.


00:31:24.957 --> 00:31:25.958
<i>No!</i>


00:31:29.261 --> 00:31:31.029
And you know,
they cut off his manhood.


00:31:35.300 --> 00:31:36.301
Mm!


00:31:38.337 --> 00:31:39.204
Mm!


00:31:49.014 --> 00:31:51.551
Got that guitar in your hand,
don't you, boy?


00:31:51.584 --> 00:31:54.987
Hey. Yeah, come on now.


00:31:55.020 --> 00:31:56.054
Hey!


00:32:16.375 --> 00:32:17.677
Hey, Cornbread!


00:32:19.779 --> 00:32:21.213
Ooh.


00:32:21.246 --> 00:32:24.551
Stack? Boy, long time no see.


00:32:24.584 --> 00:32:26.351
This here my wife, Therise.


00:32:26.385 --> 00:32:28.655
Oh, nice to meet you, Therise.


00:32:28.688 --> 00:32:30.523
Likewise.


00:32:30.557 --> 00:32:33.358
Need you to give us a moment.
Men got business to discuss.


00:32:33.392 --> 00:32:36.428
No, uh-uh. I ain't got time
for your schemin', Stack.


00:32:36.462 --> 00:32:38.263
Behind on my quota.


00:32:38.297 --> 00:32:39.465
Man, fuck your quota.


00:32:41.033 --> 00:32:42.569
This my wife right here, now.


00:32:42.602 --> 00:32:44.303
I'mma need you
to show some respect.


00:32:44.336 --> 00:32:46.004
Yeah, well,
fuck your wife, too.


00:32:49.241 --> 00:32:50.510
What's that?


00:32:50.543 --> 00:32:51.678
I said she really gonna
let you fuck her


00:32:51.711 --> 00:32:53.245
when she find out
how much money


00:32:53.278 --> 00:32:54.781
you about to get
from this job I'm offering.


00:32:54.814 --> 00:32:56.348
And none of that
nice-and-slow shit


00:32:56.381 --> 00:32:58.217
she probably giving you now.


00:32:58.250 --> 00:33:00.118
Shit, she might even let you
put your pecker in her mouth.


00:33:03.155 --> 00:33:04.591
Boy, you shoulda stayed gone,


00:33:04.624 --> 00:33:06.391
'cause I'm about to
beat the black off of you.


00:33:06.425 --> 00:33:09.394
- Come on now!
- I don't want no trouble! Hey!


00:33:09.428 --> 00:33:11.263
Well, how much money
you talkin' about payin' him?


00:33:13.298 --> 00:33:14.767
Oh, that's a good woman.


00:33:15.501 --> 00:33:16.636
Come on.


00:33:16.669 --> 00:33:17.770
We be back.


00:34:08.855 --> 00:34:10.322
Papa's here.


00:34:12.224 --> 00:34:13.793
Yeah. Papa's here.


00:34:32.912 --> 00:34:35.615
How you be?


00:34:35.648 --> 00:34:37.784
No miseries
worth complaining about.


00:34:43.856 --> 00:34:45.223
You come alone?


00:34:49.729 --> 00:34:51.664
Yeah. Stack on the other side
of town.


00:34:54.567 --> 00:34:55.568
What you come back for?


00:34:59.237 --> 00:35:01.273
We bought that old saw mill.


00:35:01.306 --> 00:35:04.877
Yeah, we gon' patch it up,
make it into a juke joint.


00:35:04.911 --> 00:35:06.478
A juke joint.


00:35:08.548 --> 00:35:10.215
This one of Stack's ideas?


00:35:10.248 --> 00:35:12.384
Yeah, he figure tonight
gonna be a grand opening.


00:35:12.417 --> 00:35:14.386
I thought y'all was done
with the Delta.


00:35:14.419 --> 00:35:16.689
Last I heard,
y'all were northern men.


00:35:16.723 --> 00:35:18.758
Nah, we through with Chicago.


00:35:18.791 --> 00:35:20.425
Chicago through with y'all?


00:35:21.728 --> 00:35:22.929
What you asking?


00:35:22.962 --> 00:35:24.864
Who you and Stack robbed


00:35:24.897 --> 00:35:26.666
to get enough money
for them crackers


00:35:26.699 --> 00:35:28.166
to sell you a whole mill?


00:35:44.316 --> 00:35:46.719
Just this, Miss Annie.


00:35:46.753 --> 00:35:48.621
And a pinch of High John.


00:35:48.655 --> 00:35:50.188
All right.


00:35:50.222 --> 00:35:53.425
Now, don't sell none of this
on the way home.


00:35:53.458 --> 00:35:55.662
I don't want your mama
comin' at me crazy later.


00:35:55.695 --> 00:35:57.229
Yes, ma'am.


00:35:57.262 --> 00:35:58.363
Thank you.


00:36:01.834 --> 00:36:04.436
I can't believe you taking
this make-believe shit.


00:36:04.469 --> 00:36:06.706
Smoke, give me my money
'fore I cut your Black ass.


00:36:06.739 --> 00:36:08.373
You can put
that blade up, woman.


00:36:10.576 --> 00:36:12.578
-I'll trade ya.
-I don't want your money.


00:36:12.612 --> 00:36:14.647
-Don't be stupid, now.
-I ain't stupid.


00:36:14.681 --> 00:36:15.815
Your money come with blood.


00:36:15.848 --> 00:36:16.949
All money
come with blood, baby.


00:36:16.983 --> 00:36:18.450
Not like yours.


00:36:18.483 --> 00:36:19.819
This shit
won't even spend nowhere else.


00:36:19.852 --> 00:36:21.386
-Look at it.
-I ain't goin' nowhere else.


00:36:21.420 --> 00:36:23.422
I don't need
that cursed money you got.


00:36:28.928 --> 00:36:30.663
You know, woman,
I been all over this world.


00:36:31.664 --> 00:36:36.435
In cars, ships, trains.


00:36:38.938 --> 00:36:42.474
I seen men die ways I didn't
even know was possible.


00:36:43.910 --> 00:36:44.944
I ain't never saw no roots,


00:36:46.612 --> 00:36:48.246
no demons...


00:36:48.280 --> 00:36:50.683
no ghosts, no magic.


00:36:52.618 --> 00:36:53.619
Just power.


00:36:55.021 --> 00:36:57.857
And only money
can get you that.


00:36:59.424 --> 00:37:01.293
You fool.


00:37:01.326 --> 00:37:02.795
All that war,


00:37:02.829 --> 00:37:06.431
or whatever the hell else
you been doin' in Chicago,


00:37:06.465 --> 00:37:09.001
and you back here
in front of me.


00:37:09.035 --> 00:37:13.338
Two arms, two legs, two eyes,
and a brain that work.


00:37:13.371 --> 00:37:15.808
How you know I ain't pray...


00:37:15.842 --> 00:37:18.376
and work every root
my grandmama taught me


00:37:18.410 --> 00:37:20.947
to keep you and that
crazy brother of yours safe


00:37:20.980 --> 00:37:22.849
every day since you been gone?


00:37:27.352 --> 00:37:29.689
So why those roots ain't work
on our baby, then?


00:37:34.459 --> 00:37:35.460
I don't know.


00:37:38.765 --> 00:37:39.999
But they work for you.


00:37:50.843 --> 00:37:52.779
You still got that mojo bag.


00:38:26.979 --> 00:38:29.081
Soil of my soil,


00:38:29.115 --> 00:38:31.651
bone of my bone,
blood of my blood.


00:38:31.684 --> 00:38:32.652
I bless you.


00:38:34.020 --> 00:38:35.021
Ashe.


00:38:52.138 --> 00:38:53.739
Why you here, Smoke?


00:38:55.041 --> 00:38:56.776
What you want with me?


00:38:59.178 --> 00:39:01.581
We was hopin' to serve food
at the juke tonight.


00:39:04.016 --> 00:39:05.551
We want you to cook for us.


00:39:07.119 --> 00:39:08.486
Elijah.


00:39:13.826 --> 00:39:15.294
You gonna make me say it?


00:39:19.165 --> 00:39:20.800
It still hurts
coming back here.


00:39:24.203 --> 00:39:25.403
But I love ya.


00:39:28.507 --> 00:39:29.575
And I miss ya.


00:41:43.743 --> 00:41:44.977
Help!


00:41:45.011 --> 00:41:46.245
Back up.


00:41:46.278 --> 00:41:48.314
Y'all gotta help.


00:41:48.347 --> 00:41:51.117
I thought I could trust them,
but they tried to kill me.


00:41:51.150 --> 00:41:52.785
-Slow down.
-Who's tryin' to kill you?


00:41:52.818 --> 00:41:54.253
Choctaw.


00:41:54.286 --> 00:41:55.788
Sure it wasn't just
some fair-skinned niggers?


00:41:55.821 --> 00:41:57.823
Ain't no Injuns around here
for miles.


00:41:59.258 --> 00:42:00.626
Oh, God.


00:42:03.929 --> 00:42:07.767
They took my wife. Oh, God.


00:42:08.934 --> 00:42:10.603
I'm a coward, ain't I?


00:42:17.076 --> 00:42:20.613
I... I got gold.


00:42:20.646 --> 00:42:22.815
Them dirty Injuns
meant to rob me.


00:42:22.848 --> 00:42:25.751
They ain't get all of it.
Y'all can have it.


00:42:25.785 --> 00:42:27.286
Just don't let 'em
hurt me no more.


00:42:54.146 --> 00:42:55.147
Evening, ma'am.


00:42:56.916 --> 00:43:01.020
We're in pursuit
of someone very dangerous.


00:43:01.053 --> 00:43:03.155
He might've come
onto your property.


00:43:03.189 --> 00:43:04.924
Have you seen anyone recently?


00:43:05.791 --> 00:43:06.792
No.


00:43:08.694 --> 00:43:10.062
Bert!


00:43:10.096 --> 00:43:11.764
Is he in there with you, ma'am?


00:43:15.234 --> 00:43:17.837
He's not what he seems.


00:43:17.870 --> 00:43:20.272
God forbid
you let him into your home.


00:43:20.306 --> 00:43:23.776
And if so, we need to act now.


00:43:52.104 --> 00:43:53.105
Bert.


00:43:54.373 --> 00:43:56.108
Injuns came and went.


00:43:58.043 --> 00:43:58.911
Bert?


00:44:08.754 --> 00:44:09.755
Bert?


00:44:17.129 --> 00:44:18.330
Bert?


00:44:22.134 --> 00:44:24.303
Oh, he's just resting.


00:44:35.881 --> 00:44:37.283
He's all better now.


00:44:38.150 --> 00:44:39.485
Hey, baby.


00:44:42.321 --> 00:44:43.455
Don't cry.


00:44:53.399 --> 00:44:54.700
Don't fall now.


00:44:56.536 --> 00:44:57.903
To the right.


00:44:57.937 --> 00:44:59.972
A little more.


00:45:00.005 --> 00:45:01.173
Oh, shit.


00:45:05.411 --> 00:45:08.080
Right this way. Ladies.


00:45:08.113 --> 00:45:10.416
Come on in!
Welcome to Club Juke.


00:45:10.449 --> 00:45:12.918
We about to get it poppin'
like fish grease, boy.


00:45:23.128 --> 00:45:26.398
We got whiskey,
Irish beer, Italian wine.


00:45:26.432 --> 00:45:28.467
Y'all some classy niggas,
ain't you?


00:45:28.500 --> 00:45:30.402
Too fancy for me.


00:45:30.436 --> 00:45:32.838
Ma'am, I don't need
no ice or nothin'.


00:45:32.871 --> 00:45:33.872
Corn liquor'll do.


00:45:33.906 --> 00:45:35.874
That'll be 50 cent.


00:45:35.908 --> 00:45:37.443
God damn, I just got 30.


00:45:37.476 --> 00:45:40.479
But these is good down
at the Maybell general store.


00:45:42.915 --> 00:45:44.984
- You like that cold, right?
- I certainly do.


00:45:45.017 --> 00:45:46.285
Comin' right up.


00:45:47.186 --> 00:45:48.954
I thank you kindly.


00:45:48.988 --> 00:45:50.356
Let me holla at y'all
right quick.


00:45:52.124 --> 00:45:54.994
- Good evenin'.
- Evenin'.


00:45:55.027 --> 00:45:56.228
You look
mighty nice.


00:45:56.262 --> 00:45:57.530
Thank you.


00:45:57.564 --> 00:45:58.831
You made it.


00:46:03.469 --> 00:46:05.204
This ain't no house party.


00:46:05.237 --> 00:46:07.139
And it damn sure
ain't no charity.


00:46:07.172 --> 00:46:10.042
We takin' cash,
US motherfuckin' dollars.


00:46:10.075 --> 00:46:11.277
This ain't Chicago, Smoke.


00:46:11.310 --> 00:46:12.579
The fuck that mean?


00:46:12.612 --> 00:46:14.179
That old nigga
worked his ass off


00:46:14.213 --> 00:46:16.015
for them wooden nickels.


00:46:16.048 --> 00:46:17.983
<i>See, these niggas been
workin' in the field all day.</i>


00:46:18.017 --> 00:46:20.252
<i>When they show up here,
let them enjoy themselves.</i>


00:46:20.286 --> 00:46:22.988
<i>They gotta feel wanted
if you want this here to work.</i>


00:46:23.022 --> 00:46:25.190
<i>This place supposed
to feel like it's for them.</i>


00:46:25.224 --> 00:46:26.225
Right this way.


00:46:27.092 --> 00:46:28.093
Uh-huh.


00:46:28.994 --> 00:46:30.462
Uh...


00:46:30.496 --> 00:46:32.464
Excuse me, ma'am.


00:46:32.498 --> 00:46:34.066
You sure
you at the right place?


00:46:34.099 --> 00:46:36.302
That's a damn good
question, Cornbread.


00:46:37.436 --> 00:46:39.071
Little Mary?


00:46:39.104 --> 00:46:40.406
Not so little no more, huh?


00:46:40.439 --> 00:46:42.609
Little Mary. Aw.


00:46:42.642 --> 00:46:44.877
When they turn
this place into a juke?


00:46:44.910 --> 00:46:46.879
We did it today.
My cousins own it.


00:46:46.912 --> 00:46:48.113
You know the Twins.


00:46:49.048 --> 00:46:50.883
Heard of 'em, of course.


00:46:50.916 --> 00:46:52.585
They your cousins?


00:46:52.619 --> 00:46:54.587
Y'all must be play cousins.


00:46:54.621 --> 00:46:57.489
Their daddy
was my daddy big brother.


00:46:57.524 --> 00:47:00.159
So y'all cousins through blood?


00:47:00.192 --> 00:47:02.995
But you seem like
such a nice young man.


00:47:03.028 --> 00:47:04.296
I ain't always nice.


00:47:05.264 --> 00:47:06.533
Ain't that young, either.


00:47:12.171 --> 00:47:15.140
My condolences
about your mother.


00:47:15.174 --> 00:47:17.076
We'd have made the repast...


00:47:18.210 --> 00:47:19.912
but me and Therise had to work.


00:47:19.945 --> 00:47:21.280
It's all right.


00:47:23.415 --> 00:47:24.584
Now let me get on in here
and get a drink


00:47:24.617 --> 00:47:26.051
before I start tearing up.


00:47:26.085 --> 00:47:27.353
Go on.
Enjoy yourself.


00:47:30.989 --> 00:47:33.425
- You got my $2?
- Huh?


00:47:35.060 --> 00:47:36.629
When you was sellin' ass
out in Little Rock...


00:47:36.663 --> 00:47:38.397
you ever let a john pay with
a goddamn promissory note?


00:47:38.430 --> 00:47:39.465
Hell no.


00:47:41.367 --> 00:47:44.403
But, see, I wasn't sellin' ass
in the Delta.


00:47:44.436 --> 00:47:45.904
You gon' play?


00:47:45.938 --> 00:47:47.139
You gon' sing?


00:47:48.608 --> 00:47:50.409
We'll see
where the night takes us.


00:47:52.645 --> 00:47:53.613
Your husband coming?


00:47:59.451 --> 00:48:00.653
Shit.


00:48:00.687 --> 00:48:01.588
Hold on.


00:48:04.256 --> 00:48:06.258
Excuse me, ma'am.


00:48:06.291 --> 00:48:07.459
I don't think
you should be here.


00:48:07.493 --> 00:48:08.961
You see, I'm with the Twins...


00:48:08.994 --> 00:48:10.462
With the Twins?


00:48:10.496 --> 00:48:12.364
Boy, if you don't
get the fuck out my face...


00:48:12.398 --> 00:48:13.666
I am with them, ma'am.


00:48:13.700 --> 00:48:15.635
We met earlier
at the train station.


00:48:15.668 --> 00:48:17.504
I'm their lil' cousin.


00:48:17.537 --> 00:48:19.071
Little cousin?


00:48:19.104 --> 00:48:20.573
I think you should leave
before they see you.


00:48:20.607 --> 00:48:22.441
Wait, you not little Sammie?


00:48:23.442 --> 00:48:24.644
The guitar.


00:48:25.978 --> 00:48:28.280
You old enough to drink now?


00:48:28.313 --> 00:48:29.915
Come on,
let me buy you a drink.


00:48:32.484 --> 00:48:34.052
-Hey, Mary.
-Grace.


00:48:34.086 --> 00:48:35.220
Good to see ya.


00:48:35.254 --> 00:48:37.089
-Two whiskeys, please.
-Sure.


00:48:37.122 --> 00:48:38.525
I don't know hoodoo,


00:48:38.558 --> 00:48:41.160
and I can't talk slick,
but I know business.


00:48:41.193 --> 00:48:43.395
And this is bad for business.


00:48:43.429 --> 00:48:44.697
It's opening night.


00:48:44.731 --> 00:48:47.032
Besides, only be
a few of 'em like this.


00:48:50.202 --> 00:48:52.371
I need
a goddamn cigarette.


00:48:52.404 --> 00:48:54.106
Comin' right up.


00:48:54.139 --> 00:48:55.575
So you play that guitar
they left you?


00:48:56.643 --> 00:48:58.578
-Yeah.
-That's good.


00:48:58.611 --> 00:49:00.312
You makin' any money
with that thing?


00:49:02.114 --> 00:49:06.185
Not really. Not yet, at least.


00:49:06.218 --> 00:49:08.020
I'd tell ya it didn't matter
as long as you love it,


00:49:08.053 --> 00:49:09.421
but that'd be horseshit advice.


00:49:14.393 --> 00:49:15.394
Hey, what are you?


00:49:17.664 --> 00:49:18.665
What am I?


00:49:20.098 --> 00:49:21.768
I'm a human being.


00:49:21.801 --> 00:49:24.604
Oh. That ain't what I meant.
I meant, more like...


00:49:24.637 --> 00:49:25.971
I know what you meant.


00:49:28.273 --> 00:49:31.511
My mama's daddy was half Black.


00:49:31.544 --> 00:49:35.180
He raised her to keep
the Klan from killing her.


00:49:35.214 --> 00:49:37.182
You know my mama
delivered the Twins?


00:49:38.183 --> 00:49:39.251
Really?


00:49:39.284 --> 00:49:40.486
She saved Stack life


00:49:40.520 --> 00:49:41.588
after he got stuck
in their mama.


00:49:41.621 --> 00:49:43.188
And after she died,


00:49:43.222 --> 00:49:44.456
my mama nursed them
like they was her own.


00:49:50.329 --> 00:49:53.733
And they had enough money
to buy this whole mill...


00:49:53.766 --> 00:49:56.502
and they ain't even
send flowers to her funeral.


00:49:56.536 --> 00:49:58.036
We sent your mama flowers.


00:49:59.204 --> 00:50:01.240
Plenty of 'em.


00:50:01.273 --> 00:50:03.275
All while she still alive
to smell 'em.


00:50:04.777 --> 00:50:06.513
- Smoke.
- Mary.


00:50:08.080 --> 00:50:09.381
Why don't you go
check in on Slim?


00:50:09.414 --> 00:50:10.783
See if he'll need backup.


00:50:29.334 --> 00:50:30.469
Take care of her or I will.


00:50:30.502 --> 00:50:32.337
No, no, I'mma handle it.
I got it.


00:50:32.371 --> 00:50:33.640
-All right, go on.
-I'm goin'.


00:50:36.676 --> 00:50:38.277
Come on. Let's go.


00:50:38.310 --> 00:50:40.078
-I'm not here for you.
-Then why you here, then?


00:50:42.147 --> 00:50:43.650
I come to hear the blues.


00:50:43.683 --> 00:50:45.183
Oh, no, they play the blues
just fine in Arkansas.


00:50:45.217 --> 00:50:46.351
Come on.


00:50:46.385 --> 00:50:47.486
Cornbread, let's get her a car.


00:50:47.520 --> 00:50:48.521
Get your hands off me.


00:50:49.889 --> 00:50:51.591
What's it gon' take?


00:50:51.624 --> 00:50:54.092
Hmm? How much to get you
to get the fuck on?


00:50:54.126 --> 00:50:56.094
You can't pay me off.


00:50:56.128 --> 00:50:57.830
Fine. I'll pay one of these
field bitches in here...


00:50:57.864 --> 00:50:59.298
to drag your ass out, then.


00:50:59.331 --> 00:51:00.800
Shit. You taught me
how to fight.


00:51:00.833 --> 00:51:02.635
I'll beat up every bitch
in here and you know it.


00:51:02.669 --> 00:51:04.704
I taught you how to walk away
when the money is up, too.


00:51:05.772 --> 00:51:07.205
Got you a rich white husband.


00:51:07.239 --> 00:51:08.675
Got you a farm.
Now go home to it.


00:51:08.708 --> 00:51:11.343
I ain't ask for none of that.


00:51:11.376 --> 00:51:13.746
All that shit was your idea.
I didn't want no white man.


00:51:13.780 --> 00:51:16.315
I didn't wanna be white.
I wanted to be with you.


00:51:16.348 --> 00:51:18.483
All it'd take is the wrong
person in here to see you...


00:51:18.518 --> 00:51:20.620
word get back to them crackers
and they gon' try to kill you.


00:51:20.653 --> 00:51:21.821
Would it matter to you?


00:51:23.590 --> 00:51:26.224
'Cause if somebody out there
put their hands on you...


00:51:26.258 --> 00:51:27.694
if they hurt you...


00:51:27.727 --> 00:51:29.596
me and my brother
gon' come kill 'em all.


00:51:29.629 --> 00:51:30.730
So you'll kill for me.


00:51:31.531 --> 00:51:32.497
That's right.


00:51:34.232 --> 00:51:37.302
But you still won't tell me
the truth.


00:51:37.336 --> 00:51:39.505
I was young enough to believe
you were comin' back.


00:51:41.574 --> 00:51:43.175
I waited.


00:51:43.208 --> 00:51:45.143
I waited a long time.


00:51:47.479 --> 00:51:50.315
But I'm grown now, Stack.


00:51:50.349 --> 00:51:51.884
And I know
you never planned to stay.


00:51:53.920 --> 00:51:55.521
Why can't you just say that?


00:51:55.555 --> 00:51:56.656
Say what?


00:51:58.256 --> 00:51:59.291
Hmm?


00:52:04.262 --> 00:52:05.497
That I love you?


00:52:10.603 --> 00:52:12.204
That I think about you
every day?


00:52:15.642 --> 00:52:17.644
I just wanted to keep you
someplace safe.


00:52:19.746 --> 00:52:21.380
And that was never
gon' be here.


00:52:24.249 --> 00:52:25.818
And that was never gon' be
with me.


00:52:27.787 --> 00:52:28.921
Never.


00:52:30.322 --> 00:52:31.323
All right.


00:53:14.834 --> 00:53:15.835
Yeah.


00:53:16.501 --> 00:53:17.502
Hey...


00:53:19.972 --> 00:53:25.511
I been hearin' about this one
particular young man all day.


00:53:25.545 --> 00:53:28.480
He 'posed to be
a bad blues man.


00:53:30.415 --> 00:53:31.984
Preacherboy, where you at?


00:53:32.018 --> 00:53:33.485
Come on here, now.


00:53:41.561 --> 00:53:44.296
That's my little cousin, y'all.
Watch this.


00:53:47.533 --> 00:53:49.702
Hold up, hold up.


00:53:49.736 --> 00:53:51.403
Tell 'em who you are,


00:53:51.436 --> 00:53:52.672
where you from.


00:53:57.710 --> 00:53:59.377
I'm Sammie Moore.


00:53:59.411 --> 00:54:01.848
- All right.
- Come on, now.


00:54:01.881 --> 00:54:06.586
I'm a sharecropper
from Sunflower plantation.


00:54:08.755 --> 00:54:10.322
They call me Preacherboy


00:54:10.355 --> 00:54:11.991
account of my daddy
being a pastor.


00:54:12.024 --> 00:54:14.292
- All right, now.
- Amen.


00:54:14.326 --> 00:54:15.728
I wrote this song for him.


00:54:15.762 --> 00:54:16.829
All right, then.


00:54:21.366 --> 00:54:23.502
<i>♪ Somethin'
I've been wanting to tell ya ♪</i>


00:54:23.536 --> 00:54:26.404
<i>♪ For a long time ♪</i>


00:54:26.438 --> 00:54:30.543
<i>♪ It might hurt you
Hope you don't lose your mind ♪</i>


00:54:30.576 --> 00:54:34.412
<i>♪ Well, I was just a boy
About eight years old ♪</i>


00:54:36.348 --> 00:54:40.052
<i>♪ Threw me a Bible
On that Mississippi road ♪</i>


00:54:40.086 --> 00:54:44.957
<i>♪ See, I love you Papa
You did all you could do ♪</i>


00:54:44.991 --> 00:54:49.729
<i>♪ They say the truth hurts
So I lied to you ♪</i>


00:54:49.762 --> 00:54:52.965
<i>♪ Yes, I lied to you
I love the blues ♪</i>


00:54:59.437 --> 00:55:00.573
Y'all move your feet now.


00:55:00.606 --> 00:55:01.574
Come on, now.


00:55:09.081 --> 00:55:10.583
Mm.


00:55:10.616 --> 00:55:11.751
<i>♪ Yeah! ♪</i>


00:55:13.052 --> 00:55:17.056
<i>♪ Somebody take me ♪</i>


00:55:17.089 --> 00:55:19.625
<i>♪ In your arms tonight ♪</i>


00:55:20.693 --> 00:55:22.762
<i>♪ Well, all right ♪</i>


00:55:22.795 --> 00:55:25.665
<i>♪ Somebody take me ♪</i>


00:55:26.866 --> 00:55:29.869
<i>♪ In your arms tonight ♪</i>


00:55:29.902 --> 00:55:32.572
<i>♪ Yeah, yeah ♪</i>


00:55:32.605 --> 00:55:36.008
<i>♪ Somebody take me ♪</i>


00:55:36.042 --> 00:55:39.712
<i>♪ In your arms tonight ♪</i>


00:55:39.745 --> 00:55:42.548
Blues wasn't forced on us
like that religion.


00:55:42.582 --> 00:55:43.816
Nah, son,


00:55:43.850 --> 00:55:45.918
we brought this
with us from home.


00:55:46.953 --> 00:55:48.988
It's magic, what we do.


00:55:49.021 --> 00:55:50.455
It's sacred...


00:55:51.591 --> 00:55:52.592
and big.


00:55:57.429 --> 00:55:59.497
<i>There are legends
of people...</i>


00:55:59.532 --> 00:56:03.468
<i>born with the gift
of making music so true...</i>


00:56:03.501 --> 00:56:08.541
<i>it can pierce the veil
between life and death.</i>


00:56:08.574 --> 00:56:10.810
<i>Conjuring spirits
from the past...</i>


00:56:10.843 --> 00:56:13.980
<i>♪ Somebody take me ♪</i>


00:56:14.013 --> 00:56:15.548
<i>...and the future.</i>


00:56:15.581 --> 00:56:16.883
<i>♪ In your arms tonight ♪</i>


00:56:18.050 --> 00:56:20.186
<i>♪ We all right ♪</i>


00:56:20.219 --> 00:56:23.923
<i>♪ Somebody take me ♪</i>


00:56:23.956 --> 00:56:26.424
<i>♪ In your arms tonight ♪</i>


00:56:29.662 --> 00:56:32.965
<i>♪ Somebody take me ♪</i>


00:56:34.166 --> 00:56:36.168
<i>♪ In your arms tonight ♪</i>


00:56:44.243 --> 00:56:47.412
New shit!
Preacherboy!


00:56:48.514 --> 00:56:49.649
Sammie Moore!


00:56:55.221 --> 00:56:57.790
<i>♪ I hope you can stand it ♪</i>


00:56:57.823 --> 00:57:00.159
<i>♪ Stand it all ♪</i>


00:57:00.192 --> 00:57:02.061
<i>♪ What I'm out here doin' ♪</i>


00:57:02.094 --> 00:57:04.664
<i>♪ You didn't preach at all ♪</i>


00:57:04.697 --> 00:57:06.999
<i>♪ See, I'm full of the blues ♪</i>


00:57:07.033 --> 00:57:09.235
<i>♪ Holy water, too ♪</i>


00:57:09.268 --> 00:57:11.604
<i>♪ I know the truth hurts ♪</i>


00:57:11.637 --> 00:57:14.006
<i>♪ So I lied to you ♪</i>


00:57:14.040 --> 00:57:16.676
<i>♪ So preacher ♪</i>


00:57:16.709 --> 00:57:18.878
<i>♪ Speak your words ♪</i>


00:57:18.911 --> 00:57:21.080
<i>♪ I know the truth hurts ♪</i>


00:57:21.113 --> 00:57:22.615
<i>♪ Yes, I lied to you ♪</i>


00:57:23.816 --> 00:57:25.885
<i>♪ I love the blues ♪</i>


00:57:25.918 --> 00:57:29.487
<i>♪ I love the blues ♪</i>


00:57:48.841 --> 00:57:52.211
<i>♪ Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah ♪</i>


00:58:00.686 --> 00:58:02.254
<i>♪ I know the truth hurts ♪</i>


00:58:03.222 --> 00:58:04.857
<i>♪ Lied to you ♪</i>


00:58:06.125 --> 00:58:10.596
<i>♪ Well, somebody take me ♪</i>


00:58:10.629 --> 00:58:15.601
<i>♪ In your arms ♪</i>


00:58:35.721 --> 00:58:37.089
<i>With this here ritual,</i>


00:58:42.728 --> 00:58:44.630
<i>we heal our people</i>


00:58:47.099 --> 00:58:48.834
<i>and we be free.</i>


00:59:36.215 --> 00:59:37.316
Do this door lock?


00:59:38.984 --> 00:59:40.853
Only with a key.


00:59:40.886 --> 00:59:42.288
Keep your foot on it, at least.


00:59:50.229 --> 00:59:53.065
Hold on. I wanna try something.


00:59:55.067 --> 00:59:56.168
Wait.


00:59:56.202 --> 00:59:58.370
Preacherboy...


00:59:58.404 --> 01:00:01.273
let me wash up first.
I walked here.


01:00:03.008 --> 01:00:04.110
You're beautiful.


01:00:05.678 --> 01:00:06.879
I just wanna taste you.


01:00:20.326 --> 01:00:21.927
Shit.


01:00:28.801 --> 01:00:30.436
Excuse me. How y'all doin'?


01:00:30.469 --> 01:00:33.372
Good? Havin' another drink?
All right now.


01:00:36.041 --> 01:00:38.010
Shit.


01:00:40.279 --> 01:00:41.447
Hey.


01:00:41.480 --> 01:00:42.882
Preacherboy!


01:00:46.952 --> 01:00:48.354
Boy found that button,
didn't he?


01:00:48.387 --> 01:00:50.389
Hey. Smoke wants ya.


01:00:50.422 --> 01:00:52.057
Check out my little cousin.


01:00:58.464 --> 01:01:01.233
He call himself,
tellin' me about the cotton.


01:01:01.267 --> 01:01:03.202
I said, "Shit...


01:01:03.235 --> 01:01:05.004
that boy
don't know nothin'..."


01:01:10.442 --> 01:01:11.710
Get the Twins.


01:01:12.878 --> 01:01:14.747
Go on. Get 'em.


01:01:14.780 --> 01:01:15.915
I tallied the till.


01:01:17.917 --> 01:01:19.351
And?


01:01:19.385 --> 01:01:20.386
What's the count?


01:01:23.355 --> 01:01:26.292
Now, that top figure,
that's plantation money.


01:01:27.459 --> 01:01:29.094
That bottom figure,


01:01:29.128 --> 01:01:30.396
that's real dollars.


01:01:32.932 --> 01:01:34.166
So what's the projection?


01:01:34.200 --> 01:01:36.468
Two months,
and we out of fresh cash.


01:01:38.137 --> 01:01:40.272
- Hey there.
- Good evening.


01:01:40.306 --> 01:01:41.840
How may I help you folks?


01:01:41.874 --> 01:01:44.310
Oh, we heard tell of a party.


01:01:44.343 --> 01:01:47.246
Drink, food, blues music
and the like.


01:01:48.013 --> 01:01:48.948
You did?


01:01:49.549 --> 01:01:51.283
We like to drink.


01:01:51.317 --> 01:01:54.386
We happen to be musicians,
and we walked here.


01:01:54.420 --> 01:01:57.122
So, we hungry as dogs.


01:01:57.156 --> 01:02:00.092
Woof woof.


01:02:00.125 --> 01:02:03.362
You wouldn't mind us
comin' in, now, would you?


01:02:03.395 --> 01:02:05.864
I think y'all
in the wrong place.


01:02:05.898 --> 01:02:07.733
What makes ya say that?


01:02:14.940 --> 01:02:16.342
You fellers
must be the owners


01:02:16.375 --> 01:02:17.843
of this establishment.


01:02:17.876 --> 01:02:19.512
That's right. And you are?


01:02:19.546 --> 01:02:21.046
Name's Remmick.


01:02:21.080 --> 01:02:23.449
This here's Joan and Bert.


01:02:23.482 --> 01:02:25.017
Hey, Stack,
y'all all right?


01:02:25.050 --> 01:02:26.352
Oh. And you...


01:02:28.354 --> 01:02:30.756
must be that voice
I heard from out here.


01:02:32.391 --> 01:02:33.526
It was beautiful.


01:02:33.560 --> 01:02:35.928
Goddamn beautiful voice.


01:02:35.961 --> 01:02:37.129
Even through these walls.


01:02:38.397 --> 01:02:39.431
Mm.


01:02:40.432 --> 01:02:41.800
Where y'all from?


01:02:41.834 --> 01:02:43.035
Just down the road.


01:02:43.068 --> 01:02:44.270
And how far is that?


01:02:44.303 --> 01:02:45.404
North Carolina.


01:02:45.437 --> 01:02:47.406
-Y'all Klan?
-Sir...


01:02:49.275 --> 01:02:52.011
We believe
in equality.


01:02:52.044 --> 01:02:53.879
And music.


01:02:53.912 --> 01:02:55.481
We just came here to play.


01:02:55.515 --> 01:02:57.783
Spend some money,
have a good time.


01:02:59.251 --> 01:03:00.319
Here, I'll show you.


01:03:04.923 --> 01:03:06.392
<i>♪ I... ♪</i>


01:03:06.425 --> 01:03:08.427
<i>♪ Pick poor Robin clean ♪</i>


01:03:08.460 --> 01:03:10.362
<i>♪ Pick poor Robin clean ♪</i>


01:03:10.396 --> 01:03:13.465
<i>♪ I picked his head
I picked his feet ♪</i>


01:03:13.499 --> 01:03:16.335
<i>♪ I would've picked his body
But he wasn't fit to eat ♪</i>


01:03:16.368 --> 01:03:20.939
<i>♪ I pick poor Robin clean
Pick poor Robin clean ♪</i>


01:03:22.509 --> 01:03:24.310
<i>♪ And I'll be satisfied
Having a family ♪</i>


01:03:24.343 --> 01:03:25.944
These pecks ain't bad.


01:03:25.978 --> 01:03:28.881
<i>♪ Lord, didn't that
Jaybird laugh ♪</i>


01:03:28.914 --> 01:03:32.084
<i>♪ When I picked
Poor Robin clean ♪</i>


01:03:32.117 --> 01:03:35.954
<i>♪ Poor Robin clean
I picked poor Robin clean ♪</i>


01:03:35.988 --> 01:03:38.525
<i>♪ Lord, didn't that
Jaybird laugh ♪</i>


01:03:38.558 --> 01:03:40.426
All right, all right, hold on,


01:03:40.459 --> 01:03:41.561
<i>-hold on. Just a minute.
-♪ When I picked poor Ro... ♪</i>


01:03:41.594 --> 01:03:43.295
It's just about to get good.


01:03:43.329 --> 01:03:45.565
Nah, I believe ya,
but this here a juke joint.


01:03:45.598 --> 01:03:46.599
Blues music.


01:03:46.633 --> 01:03:48.100
But we got money,


01:03:48.133 --> 01:03:49.301
and we ready to
spend it with y'all.


01:03:49.335 --> 01:03:50.469
Sounding damn near perfect


01:03:50.502 --> 01:03:51.937
and you're saying
we ain't welcome?


01:03:51.970 --> 01:03:53.305
No, I'm saying you get down
that road


01:03:53.339 --> 01:03:55.307
and get back into town.


01:03:55.341 --> 01:03:57.309
Plenty of white barrelhouses
down there.


01:03:59.278 --> 01:04:00.913
This 'cause we're...


01:04:02.414 --> 01:04:03.415
All right.


01:04:04.617 --> 01:04:06.285
How'd she get in?


01:04:06.318 --> 01:04:08.987
-Now, that is none of...
-She here 'cause she family.


01:04:09.021 --> 01:04:10.122
Family.


01:04:13.158 --> 01:04:15.361
Can't we just, for one night...


01:04:16.596 --> 01:04:18.063
just all be family?


01:04:19.331 --> 01:04:21.601
You don't need to do that, sir.


01:04:21.634 --> 01:04:23.102
We'll be on our way.


01:04:26.438 --> 01:04:29.141
But we're gonna walk real slow.


01:04:29.174 --> 01:04:31.009
Just in case
y'all change your mind.


01:04:37.684 --> 01:04:39.519
Y'all have a nice night.


01:04:44.056 --> 01:04:45.424
They gave me
the willies.


01:04:45.457 --> 01:04:46.425
Yeah, well,
crackers at nighttime


01:04:46.458 --> 01:04:47.493
will do that to you.


01:04:47.527 --> 01:04:49.596
Wasn't just that.


01:04:49.629 --> 01:04:51.063
You think they brought company?


01:04:51.096 --> 01:04:52.398
I doubt it.


01:04:52.431 --> 01:04:54.333
But we got enough pepper
on us if they did.


01:04:54.366 --> 01:04:56.135
Shit, we forgot the trunk.


01:04:56.168 --> 01:04:57.336
Man, why ain't you remind me?


01:04:57.369 --> 01:04:59.338
Fool, I told you to remind me.


01:04:59.371 --> 01:05:02.207
Y'all don't need the trunk.
There was just three of 'em.


01:05:03.208 --> 01:05:04.511
Now listen to me,


01:05:04.544 --> 01:05:06.546
what if they just came to sing?


01:05:06.579 --> 01:05:08.615
And what if somebody
spill somethin' on 'em?


01:05:08.648 --> 01:05:10.182
Step on their shoe?


01:05:10.215 --> 01:05:11.950
Look at their woman
a bit too long?


01:05:11.984 --> 01:05:14.420
We gon' have a bigger problem
than just a fight.


01:05:14.453 --> 01:05:15.421
Sure do.


01:05:16.422 --> 01:05:17.557
Don't let them in.


01:05:40.279 --> 01:05:41.447
They said you wanna talk.


01:05:41.480 --> 01:05:42.715
Yeah.


01:05:42.749 --> 01:05:44.216
Seen your performance
down there.


01:05:44.249 --> 01:05:45.317
Pretty damn good.


01:05:47.052 --> 01:05:48.487
Can't thank you
enough for this.


01:05:50.389 --> 01:05:52.458
I mean, y'all the ones who
put that guitar in my hand.


01:05:53.425 --> 01:05:55.494
Now this.


01:05:55.528 --> 01:05:57.329
Well, you got the talent.
That's for certain.


01:05:57.362 --> 01:06:00.466
But all this
ain't no life for nobody.


01:06:00.499 --> 01:06:03.368
I know plenty musicians.
I ain't never met a happy one.


01:06:04.269 --> 01:06:05.538
Yeah, it's cute now.


01:06:05.572 --> 01:06:06.706
But it get old.


01:06:07.674 --> 01:06:09.408
That ramblin'.


01:06:09.441 --> 01:06:11.544
I mean,
being with y'all today...


01:06:13.546 --> 01:06:15.080
Smoke, I feel like I'm flying.


01:06:16.181 --> 01:06:18.083
Well, today settled it.


01:06:18.116 --> 01:06:19.318
I'm headin' off on my own.


01:06:20.385 --> 01:06:21.621
Where you goin'?


01:06:21.654 --> 01:06:22.589
I don't know.


01:06:24.456 --> 01:06:26.726
-Maybe Chicago.
-Hmm.


01:06:26.759 --> 01:06:28.126
What's wrong, Stack?


01:06:28.160 --> 01:06:29.261
We underwater.


01:06:29.294 --> 01:06:31.330
How?


01:06:31.363 --> 01:06:33.600
All the plantations down there
payin' with credits.


01:06:36.201 --> 01:06:37.336
What about them crackers?


01:06:37.369 --> 01:06:39.071
What about 'em?


01:06:39.104 --> 01:06:40.673
I can go feel 'em out
before they're too far gone.


01:06:40.707 --> 01:06:43.308
I could feel 'em out myself.


01:06:43.342 --> 01:06:45.612
They'll tell me more
than they'll tell you.


01:06:45.645 --> 01:06:47.279
And I can find out
what they really have.


01:06:47.312 --> 01:06:48.648
And what happens
if they're from Little Rock?


01:06:48.681 --> 01:06:50.115
They ain't.


01:06:50.148 --> 01:06:53.118
One day our daddy
beat Stack real bad.


01:06:53.151 --> 01:06:55.822
So we get in our minds
that we need to run away.


01:06:55.855 --> 01:06:58.390
See, me, I wanna go
to the next plantation over.


01:06:58.423 --> 01:06:59.692
But Stack,


01:06:59.726 --> 01:07:01.460
he figure
we get to Mound Bayou.


01:07:01.493 --> 01:07:04.162
Small town.
Right here in Mississippi.


01:07:04.196 --> 01:07:06.098
Founded by free slaves.


01:07:06.131 --> 01:07:08.267
And everything is Black-owned.


01:07:09.134 --> 01:07:10.202
That sound like a crock.


01:07:10.235 --> 01:07:12.237
Yeah, well, I seen it.


01:07:12.271 --> 01:07:13.773
Why y'all ain't stay?


01:07:13.806 --> 01:07:16.308
That mayor knew
who our daddy was.


01:07:16.341 --> 01:07:18.277
Knew he was a evil man.


01:07:18.310 --> 01:07:19.679
Figured it was no way


01:07:19.712 --> 01:07:22.582
that he ain't passed
that evil down to us.


01:07:22.615 --> 01:07:24.651
<i>Let me go
get this money for us.</i>


01:07:24.684 --> 01:07:26.151
I know y'all need it.


01:07:26.184 --> 01:07:27.419
And what's that
supposed to mean?


01:07:27.452 --> 01:07:29.522
See, your daddy a preacher.


01:07:29.556 --> 01:07:31.423
You can go and do that.


01:07:31.456 --> 01:07:34.293
You like makin' music?
Make church music.


01:07:34.326 --> 01:07:36.094
You wan' leave...


01:07:36.128 --> 01:07:37.830
go on down Mound Bayou.


01:07:37.864 --> 01:07:40.600
Live with the proper
Black folks.


01:07:40.633 --> 01:07:43.603
Leave all this here
improper shit to us.


01:07:43.636 --> 01:07:44.604
Irish beer?


01:07:45.572 --> 01:07:46.839
Italian wine?


01:07:47.807 --> 01:07:49.107
You rob both sides.


01:07:49.141 --> 01:07:50.375
Let 'em blame each other


01:07:50.409 --> 01:07:51.544
while you and Smoke
come down here


01:07:51.578 --> 01:07:52.845
and set up shop.


01:07:52.879 --> 01:07:54.581
You gon' need
every dime you can get


01:07:54.614 --> 01:07:55.748
when they put
two and two together.


01:07:55.782 --> 01:07:57.115
But they won't.


01:07:57.149 --> 01:07:58.483
They might.


01:07:58.518 --> 01:07:59.819
Well, I ain't goin'
to Mound Bayou.


01:07:59.852 --> 01:08:01.754
My daddy a reverend,


01:08:01.788 --> 01:08:03.556
but I'm y'all cousin, too.


01:08:03.590 --> 01:08:06.224
